# Security invariants (permanent)

When touching APIs, media fetch, uploads, or `proxy.ts`:

## Must keep

- Mutations under `/api/admin`, `/api/studio`, `/api/accountant` go through `rejectCrossSiteMutation` via `pathRequiresCsrf` in `proxy.ts` (login paths exempt).
- Outbound image/URL fetch: `assertPublicHttpUrlResolved` and/or `fetchTrustedImageBytes` / `trustedImageToDataUrl` — never bare `fetch` to caller-supplied URLs.
- Uploads: `normalizeUploadContentType` / `ALLOWED_UPLOAD_MIME` from `lib/upload-mime` (fed by `lib/truth/security`). Block SVG/HTML.
- Client HTML: `sanitizeHtmlForClientPreview`; strip `data:image/svg+xml`.
- Token downloads: rate-limit helpers; respect `finalPackageExpiresAt`.

## Must not

- Remove CSRF from `proxy.ts` matcher or `pathRequiresCsrf`.
- Add `image/svg+xml` to upload allowlists.
- Follow open redirects in maps/IG/media helpers without host allowlists.
- Clobber Google Sheet formula cells from Apps Script / sheet tools.

Source of truth: `brightline/lib/truth/security.ts` + `brightline/lib/truth/truth.test.ts`.
